course: dictionary
lesson: 9368
title: Spooks, ghosts and startled horses
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The meaning you choose depends on the words around it, which is its context. «Riders wear helmets on every horse, even a quiet pony, because any horse may spook at a bag or a bird and throw its rider.» Here spook means suddenly take fright. Ask yourself: what does the horse do, and why does it matter?
explain: Spook can also be a ghost in a Halloween story, or a spy in a film. Read the whole sentence to find which meaning fits. A ghost is not likely to be a bag or a bird, so the horse sense is the right one here.
explain: Spook can be a verb too. To spook someone or an animal is to frighten or startle them suddenly. Spooked is the past tense: the horse was spooked. Spooky is an adjective: a spooky house is one that makes you feel scared.
fact: Spook means a ghost, especially in informal English.
fact: To spook an animal is to frighten or startle it suddenly, so it may run off.
fact: Spook can also mean a spy, mostly in informal American English, as in a spy film.
fact: «Spooky» is an adjective that describes something that feels like a ghost or is scary.
fact: Never use spook as an insult or to describe people. It is an unkind word for people.
exercise: «Riders wear helmets on every horse, even a quiet pony, because any horse may spook at a bag or a bird.» What does spook mean here? | Eat its food | *Suddenly take fright | Run a slow race | Fall fast asleep
exercise: In a Halloween story, the spook floated through the wall. What is a spook in this story? | *A ghost | A bird | A rider's helmet | A pony's saddle
exercise: Find and copy the word that means frighten or startle suddenly. «The loud bang spooked the cows in the field.» | loud | field | *spooked | bang
test: «The old house looked spooky in the moonlight.» What word describes the house? | helmet | startled | pony | *spooky
test: In a spy film, the spooks met in a secret room. What are the spooks in this film? | Horses | *Secret agents | Ghosts | Helmets
exam: Why do riders wear helmets, according to «Riders wear helmets on every horse»? | *Because a horse may spook and throw its rider, and helmets prevent serious head injuries | To make the horse run faster | To keep the horse warm | To look smart at a show
